+## Everything else that went with them
+
+Recovered the same day, from the same commit:
+
+| Where | What |
+|---|---|
+| `asc_soma/corpus/` | 43 tools: every specialist's corpus builder, the fetchers for GOV.UK, Hansard, the NHS vocabulary and the dictionary, the British-English normaliser, the typo augmenter, coverage and language-cost measurement, held-out panel builders |
+| `asc_soma/domains/` | the 15 declaration modules the `soma.toml` files were generated from |
+| `asc_soma/teacher/` | the five teacher-cache tools |
+| `asc_soma/derive/` | the five trace derivers, and their 35 tests, which pass |
+| `packages/soma/lab-results/` | the Stage-A and Stage-B run logs, the gate, energy and probe logs, and the LFS pointers for `schema-author.sm.pt` and its sidecars |
+
+The `.pt` files were Git LFS pointers rather than weights, so what was in the
+repository is what came back; whether the objects behind them still exist in the
+LFS store is a separate question worth checking.
+
+Most of `corpus/` and all of `teacher/` still import `soma_paths`, `domains` or
+the old `soma` module and will not run until those are repointed. They are
+recovered so the work exists rather than presented as working.
